# Overview
#
# A closing cliche ends a section without saying anything (`The
# possibilities are endless`, `You're all set`). The reader learns
# nothing from the last line of the section. The fix deletes the cliche
# and ends the section on its last fact. The rule sits at Recommended,
# because the pattern cannot tell where a section ends, so it matches
# each phrase anywhere in the text.
#
# Expression
#
# The entry for `only time will tell` puts `only` in a list of one word,
# so check.py does not read it as a plain entry. check.py fails a plain
# entry that holds a shorter one, because the shorter entry already
# matches every sentence that the longer one matches. Here the longer
# entry moves the start of the finding to `only`, so the fix deletes the
# whole phrase instead of leaving `Only` behind.
#
# False Positives
#
# A phrase in the middle of a section still draws a finding (`The parser
# reads one token, and if that's it, the parser returns`). `time will
# tell` also draws a finding where `time` counts a run (`the second time
# will tell you which cache is stale`).
#
# Related Rules
#
# ProseFutureTense skips `time will tell`, so only this rule reports the
# phrase, with or without `only` before it.
#
# Measurement
#
# The rule hit 2 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 2 of 2 sampled hits
# said nothing. Each one was `that's it!` after a code block. One
# opened the last paragraph of its section, and the other sat in the
# middle of its section. `time will tell` did not hit any line in the
# corpus, so no sample measures that phrase.
expr main [(the future looks bright), (time will tell), ([only] time will tell), (exciting times ahead), (the possibilities are endless), (that's it), (you're all set), (you are all set), (say goodbye to)]
let message "Closing cliche. Delete it and end on the last fact."
let description "Flags cliches that end a section without saying anything."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
test "Only time will tell whether the API sticks." " whether the API sticks."
allows "The event log records every retry."
